Sandbox policy (linux)
Mode: workspace-write (workspace-write: commands and file tools may write only below the write roots)
Write roots:
- /home/dev/proj (workspace)
- /srv/shared/out (grant)
- /home/dev/.dsh/scratch/s-policy (scratch)
Network: allowed
Escalation: If the sandbox denies an action you need, retry that exact call once with sandbox_permissions set to a wider mode and a justification; a person decides, and only that one call is widened.
Platform note: /tmp is writable only when it is a write root.
